From 2d6c23e2a53824152fec61020c275859fb1693da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alemar <6304136+darkguy2008@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:18:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] kconfig: keep strrchr()'s result const in conf_write()

glibc 2.43 makes strrchr() return a const pointer when it is passed a
const string (C23 qualifier-preserving search functions), so gcc warns
when building the host kconfig tools:

  scripts/kconfig/confdata.c:758:35: warning: assignment discards 'const'
  qualifier from pointer target type [-Wdiscarded-qualifiers]

conf_write() only reads through slash, so declare it const.

Signed-off-by: Alemar <6304136+darkguy2008@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 scripts/kconfig/confdata.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c b/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c
index 08e75599..281fe2a0 100644
--- a/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c
+++ b/scripts/kconfig/confdata.c
@@ -749,7 +749,7 @@ int conf_write(const char *name)
 	dirname[0] = 0;
 	if (name && name[0]) {
 		struct stat st;
-		char *slash;
+		const char *slash;
 
 		if (!stat(name, &st) && S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)) {
 			strcpy(dirname, name);
-- 
